      "content": "Your observations are astute and could indeed be indicative of a targeted approach. When you consult with a lawyer, they will look for evidence of intentional acts that could be construed as creating a hostile work environment or constructive dismissal. The shift from a friendly to a formal tone in communications, especially if it coincides with other negative changes, could suggest a deliberate attempt to alienate you. The lawyer will likely examine the timing, frequency, and nature of these communications, as well as any direct or indirect references to your performance or presence in the workplace. They will also consider the broader context, such as any recent changes in company policy or personnel that may have affected you disproportionately. Your meticulous documentation will be crucial in establishing a pattern of behavior that supports your claim. Remember, the law is on your side, and with the right evidence, you can shine a light on the truth and seek justice for your situation.",
